\section{Reference semantics}{

A WRite document is \strong{modified in place}: each modification function
changes the object and returns it invisibly, which allows chaining calls
with \verb{|>}. Use \code{\link[=doc_copy]{doc_copy()}} to work on an independent copy. The original
file is never modified unless \code{\link[=doc_save]{doc_save()}} overwrites it.
}

\section{Illustration notation}{

The "Illustration" sections of the help pages represent the document as text:
\itemize{
\item one line = one paragraph;
\item \verb{[name: text]} = the bookmark \code{name} surrounding \code{text} (\verb{[name: ]} = empty bookmark);
\item \verb{**text**} = bold text, \verb{<page break>} = page break,
\verb{<image>} = image, \verb{| a | b |} = table row.
}
}

